 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Immerse yourself in the language. Watch movies, listen to music, and try to follow the script or lyrics as you go. A good language learnt by osmosis. Start with a hundred most common words, then build from there. A list tells you which words come next, which helps remembering. Stick to simple novels with lot of images. If you find yourself stopping to look up words every page, try something simpler. They' great for beginners. The pictures help you follow the story, and words are usually simple.",
